<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · song</p><h1 class="enc-title">Redemption Song</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">written c. 1979; released <a href="/years/1980">1980</a> on the album Uprising</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">&quot;Redemption <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song</a>&quot; is the last track of Uprising, the twelfth album of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bob-marley">Bob Marley</a> and the Wailers, produced by Chris Blackwell and released by Island Records in 1980. It is reported to have been written around 1979 and first appears on a demo tape known as the &quot;<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dada">Dada</a> Demos&quot;.</p></div>
